 "the order in which we place the COs doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t seem to matter \
(idempotent) (",
 StyleBox["prove this",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "), but where those COs are placed does - need a local model?\n-> no COs \
disappear, so regardless of how many COs have already been placed, placing \
another at most only \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]swaps\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
those COs onto a different chromatid, so the number of COs is unaffected.\n\
this goes for CO visibility as well - placement of another CO never renders \
the original CO invisible."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990546825982794*^9, 3.990546886353095*^9}, {
  3.9905484806096773`*^9, 3.9905485115790253`*^9}, {3.99054866847692*^9, 
  3.990548714423834*^9}, {3.9905488483365307`*^9, 3.990548868804357*^9}, {
  3.99054891156468*^9, 
  3.990548914341864*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"64d9c46f-f302-480e-bae8-\
45e8a8fdc83e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
order of CO placements doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t matter if relative ordering \
is consistent?\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990559317622322*^9, 3.990559335117085*^9}, {
   3.99055939462889*^9, 3.99055939749689*^9}, {3.990560521302021*^9, 
