4e6c778b4d7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["why does ordering not matter in one case, but does matter in the \
other case?\n",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 StyleBox["-> ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "in one of them, you only ever cross to a non-sister haplotype, but in the \
other, you could be crossing to a sister haplotype!!\nso CO order DOES matter \
- that\[CloseCurlyQuote]s another thing to disentangle.\nhow do we handle CO \
ordering? each order has equal likelihood => divide prob by number of orders\n\
how do we determine what resulting chromatids we can get from diff orders?"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990564727336113*^9, 3.9905647418993397`*^9}, {
  3.990565015856647*^9, 3.990565044416952*^9}, {3.9905651784118443`*^9, 
  3.990565196475917*^9}, {3.990575980537168*^9, 
  3.990576016705392*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"40b9aeca-6c24-4a04-87d3-\
e8da75b7c9c7"],

Cell["\<\
the relative ordering of the COs from the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]anchor end\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] of the CO matters, but as long as that\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s kept consistent, ordering of COs doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
matter.
more accurately: ordering doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t matter, but location \
matters. how do we factor in location?
exact location doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t matter, but relative ordering does.
-> rules for how relative ordering affects haplotypes?
-> mathematically determine orderings?\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9905604205257072`*^9, 3.990560481789773*^9}, {
  3.9905606470013933`*^9, 3.990560674778262*^9}, {3.990560887649454*^9, 
  3.990560921936159*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5aa805b8-3127-4569-a8d8-\
46bb9706a9d2"],

Cell["\<\
one idea: each CO\[CloseCurlyQuote]s location represented by PDF over length \
of chromatid?\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990560926995224*^9, 
  3.990560953616172*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a617da9f-5910-46f1-8916-\
456d27b0ed8a"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
